    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI want to comment out the current line in insert mode, so I mapped `<C-#>` in insert mode to `<C-o>:lua MiniComment.operator(\"line\")<CR>`.\r\nHowever, when executing this, my cursor does not move the appropriate amount of characters to the right / left because of the added / removed characters.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\ncomment line with `lua MiniComment.operator(\"line\")`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nthe cursor should move with line content\r\n- when there is text on the line the cursor should be at the same position in that text (relative to content, not absolute)\r\n- when there is none, the cursor should be at the end of the line, not at the front\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nthe cursor stays at the same character number, not relative to the text\r\n![bug demonstration](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/64850647/193250168-4df77e57-6d6c-4553-bc54-6e0679b9ca4e.gif)\r\n\r\n",
